      "content": "Yes, economic models do indicate a potential short-term dip in portfolio value as rising rates increase the cost of borrowing and trigger selling pressure on equities. While a temporary decline is anticipated, it is exceedingly rare for a well-diversified portfolio to drop more than 5-10% within a single six-month period. Unless your assets are highly concentrated in risk-free bonds now, your future expenses should remain safely covered even if your account balance fluctuates slightly. You might consider rebalancing to reduce equity exposure rather than moving everything to cash, as this strategy can mitigate risk while still allowing you to capture future growth.",
